# The tokens Face Yourself creates enter at the same time and see each other enter (the ruling; CR 101.4, 603.2c). Bot2
# cast Grizzly Bears and then Rampaging Ferocidon ("Whenever another creature enters, this creature deals 1 damage to
# that creature's controller"), so the Bears copy is made before the Ferocidon copy, the order a one-at-a-time loop would
# use, in which the new Ferocidon would never see the new Bears enter. Bot1's life: Bot2's Ferocidon sees both tokens enter
# (2 damage) and Bot1's Ferocidon token sees the Bears token enter (1 more): 17.
[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus x3
Face Yourself
Mountain x3
Mountain x10
[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus x2
Grizzly Bears
Rampaging Ferocidon
Forest x4
Forest x10
[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot2.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot2.Hand.Rampaging Ferocidon.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Face Yourself.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 2
? Bot1.Life = 17
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 17
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 0
